#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only the ‘open’ tiles can be selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"‘Open’ tile is the tile which has one of the tile’s vertical sides open, "
"meaning that on other tiles are located immediately next to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only then matching, open tiles can be removed from the game board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Matching tiles are such tiles where the face pictograms match exactly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are exceptions to this rule! In the traditional game of Mahjong each "
"tile has a matching one except for the ‘Flowers’ and ‘Seasons’ tiles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The ‘Flowers’ tiles have no doubles in the set and can be matched directly "
"to each-other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The ‘Seasons’ tiles have no doubles in the set and can be matched directly "
"to each-other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not every instance of the KMahjongg game can be finished. Sometimes the "
"tiles are mixed in such a way that it may not be possible to find all the "
"matches. This problem can be avoided. Please refer to this section of the …"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To be eligible for a place amongst the high scores player has to complete a "
"game instance within the shortest period of time possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the player uses ‘cheat’ feature his/here record will not be considered as "
"a high Score."
msgstr ""

